					},
					"text": {
						"type": "string",
						"value": "EXAMPLE: VECTOR TO ANGLE\n\nIn this example we've got a randomly rotating dot, controlled by the Perlin Generator node.\nThe result of sine and cosine from that value dictacte float2 position of the dot.\nWe use that same vector in the Atan 2 node to get the angle from 0 to that vector (in radians).\nThe Angle Converter node is used to convert from radians to period (which the Transform node wants)."
					}
				},
				"bounds": {
					"height": 848.22625732421875,
					"width": 1976.3388671875,
					"x": -31.12655258178710938,
					"y": 502.6923828125
				},
				"class": {
					"id": "77697265-3C1D-467D-A722-0FC566538374",
					"version": 1
				},
				"clock": "video",
				"color": "ffff6a00",
